// "Draw N" ([CR#121.1]): the imperative YOU-form draw — you draw N cards, ONE
// AT A TIME ([CR#121.2] — a per-card sequence, NOT a simultaneous batch like
// mill). Scry's sibling on the draw lane, the twin of `Mill`: the keyword
// action as DATA — a `Composite` whose tag is `Draw(You, n)` and whose body
// DESCRIBES the top-N Library → Hand relocation (an `Each` per-card move). The
// engine does NOT run the body: it emits N independent single-card `Act(Draw)`
// attempts, each of which binds the library top LATE and empty-checks BEFORE
// its move (an empty library loses the game, [CR#120.3,104.3c] — an executing
// `Each` body would silently no-op and MISS that loss). The declarative-subject
// form ("Target player draws N cards.") is the `Draws(who, n)` macro; this is
// the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Draw(1) -> "Draw a card." / Draw(3) -> "Draw three cards."
(
    name: "Draw",
    template: "draw ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Count],
    body: Composite(
        Draw(You, Param(0)),
        Each(binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: Param(0))), effect: Move(It, Hand)),
    ),
)
